 "text": "Hey, good to have you back. How have you been? A balanced meal plan is easy when you start with a few foundation foods. Give rice, pasta, oats, edamame and peas and berries as many ways as you can think of. That's fine, but try to introduce new versions of it all week. Cook some with chicken, have some with dal, have some in a sauce. That's fine on day she's not eating. A big bowl of cereal with milk and fruit is easy and gives you mornings free. Letting little ones help is magical, but keep them in gloves or a kitchen apron. Start with pouring the cereal and work your way up.",
